I see the issue - when `fgetc` returns EOF, the loop exits but then I check if `buf->len == saved_len && ferror(fp)`. If no bytes were read AND there's an error, return false. But when we reach EOF normally (no error), `ferror(fp)` is 0, so it returns true even though we're at EOF. The problem is that the loop exits on EOF but then I'm returning true which causes another iteration.

The issue is: when we hit EOF without reading any new bytes, we should return false to signal end-of-file. Let me fix this:
